Key Observations
	Age is the strongest predictor (top split, highest importance variable)
	Hypertension, Glucose level, and BMI are major contributors (branches, node splits)
	Cross-validation error increased as tree became more complex  possible overfitting
	Smoking and residence type had weak influence (low importance scores)
	Overall, the results support our earlier logistic regression findings where age had the strongest statistical significance.
